msgid "intro/description/banPhase"
msgstr ""
"Each team can completely ban a vehicle from a battle. Coordinate votes with "
"allies to exclude your most feared machine or to prepare an unexpected "
"lineup for enemies. If your vehicle is banned, you can choose from several "
"pre-configured rentals instead."

msgid "intro/description/draw"
msgstr ""
"When the timer expires and no team has achieved a clear victory, the battle "
"outcome is decided by tiebreakers in this order: surviving vehicles, damage "
"dealt, and the first vehicle defeated. If no damage is dealt by either team,"
" the battle is declared a draw."

msgid "intro/description/nightMaps"
msgstr ""
"Night Maps refresh familiar battlefields with nighttime conditions, new "
"Observation Posts, updated POIs, and modified spotting mechanics. The "
"current lineup includes Glacier, Sand River, Outpost, and Steppes."

msgid "intro/description/onslaughtModifiers"
msgstr ""
"The mode has modifiers that change certain parameters of the vehicle, such "
"as vehicle hit points, consumables cooldown time, time remaining visible, "
"and more."

msgid "intro/description/pointsOfInterest"
msgstr ""
"Once you capture certain areas of the map, you'll gain access to Tactical "
"Skills. There are two types of points of interest: Artillery Headquarters, "
"which let you call in a targeted strike, and Comms Centers, which reveal all"
" enemy vehicles. The number and location of these sites vary from map to "
"map."

msgid "intro/description/qualification"
msgid_plural "plural/intro/description/qualification"
msgstr[0] ""
"Fight %(count)s Qualification battle to determine your skill level and rank. Upon completion, you will receive rewards for the rank you achieved and all previous ranks.\n"
"\n"
"Desertion or a draw in Qualification will be considered as a defeat."
msgstr[1] ""
"Fight %(count)s Qualification battles to determine your skill level and rank. Upon completion, you will receive rewards for the rank you achieved and all previous ranks.\n"
"\n"
"Desertion or a draw in Qualification will be considered as a defeat."
msgstr[2] ""
"Fight %(count)s Qualification battles to determine your skill level and rank. Upon completion, you will receive rewards for the rank you achieved and all previous ranks.\n"
"\n"
"Desertion or a draw in Qualification will be considered as a defeat."

msgid "intro/description/ranks"
msgstr ""
"Progress through the ranks from Iron to Legend and earn valuable prizes. "
"Fight throughout the Year of the Phoenix to receive unique Annual Rewards."

msgid "intro/description/roleSkills"
msgstr ""
"Depending on the role, each vehicle has a special skill with three charge levels. The higher the charge level when the skill is activated, the stronger the effect will be. The charge level will depend on the number of Prestige Points that can be earned for impressive performance in battle, capturing Points of Interest, using Tactical Skills, etc.\n"
"\n"
"Check out the mode regulations to learn more about the different ways you can earn Prestige Points."

msgid "intro/description/vehiclesOnMap"
msgstr ""
"You can enter battle in Tier %(levels)s researchable vehicles (excluding "
"SPGs), as well as Collectors' and some special vehicles. Prepare your "
"vehicles in the Garage, then choose the best one based on the features of "
"the given map once you get into battle. When selecting your vehicle, also "
"consider which vehicles your allies have chosen."

